      "writtenOn": "2019-01-31T03:19:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You are definitely right. The streaming container cannot grab sgi-net IP address of ngic-dp. This IP address is not used when cdn_update is false, which is default configuration. In cdn.yaml file, you can see that spgw_sgi_ip is not referred. This variable is only referred when cdn_update is true. The reason why I define this value is that we can dynamically set spgw_sgi_ip address when redeploying mcord-data-plane (e.g., helm upgrade --set cdn_update\u003dtrue --set spgw_sgi_ip\u003d13.1.1.84 ...). \n\nOnce we deploy ngic-dp container, the sgi-net IP address for ngic-dp is not changed for a while even after the redeployment. With this feature, we can explicitly assign sgi-net IP address of ngic-dp into spgw_sgi_ip. Then, streaming container has more detailed routing rule (e.g., the results of \"route -n\" command).\n\nIf default commands in cdn.yaml does not work (i.e., ping b/w UE and streaming server does not work due to the routing rule), we initially figure out the sgi-net ip address of ngic-dp. Then, we can redeploy mcord-data-plane with the command \"helm upgrade --set cdn_update\u003dtrue --set spgw_sgi_ip\u003d13.1.1.84 ...\". If the default command works, it would be better.\n\nIf it is still confusing, please text me through slack :).",
